    <string name="fact_saffron">The dried stigmas of a crocus flower, picked by hand at dawn. About 150 flowers are needed for a single gram.</string>
    <string name="fact_paprika">Sweet peppers dried slowly over oak smoke, then stone ground. The deepest red grades are the mildest ones.</string>
    <string name="fact_cinnamon">The inner bark of a laurel tree, rolled into quills while it is still damp so it curls as it dries.</string>
    <string name="fact_cumin">Ridged seeds toasted in a dry pan until they crackle. One minute too long and the warmth turns bitter.</string>
    <string name="fact_cardamom">Green pods holding black seeds, the third costliest spice after saffron and vanilla. Crush the pod, never the seed.</string>

